abstract: "705 runs of an agent-based simulation of how authority concentrates in a network of nodes that assert, contest and settle claims under six swappable governance primitives. Every run carries its full configuration, a scorecard of ~40 outcome metrics, a provenance record of the engine version that produced it, and its place in the lab's cohort / hypothesis structure. The archive is offered as a testbed for how independent research agents surface conflicting assumptions without a central reconciler, keeping the disagreement and the provenance rather than collapsing them."
